Z||000005||KRMFiero||04-01-2001||09:33 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by jch82:<BR><B>What did you do to get the 120speedo to read the correct speed?? I always thought you had to do something else besides just swapping it in?? Lemme know cuz I want to do this also...Thanks<P>Josh   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I am also looking for a 120 speedo BUT, i am almost 100% positive that the gears and eveything are the same its just a crystal or somethign in the speedo that calibrates it or something, im not sure but i know it is plug and play  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/tongue.gif"><P>Kyle||||reg||1
Z||000006||WKDFIRO||04-02-2001||01:46 AM||||You can manually take the reading and reset it. Its very easy when you look at it. I did 120 for my 85 GT and it blew me away how easy it was to alter the mileage. <P>Makes me wonder about some of these low mileage Fieros....<P>I did no adjustments to the gauge other than the miles. It seems to read just fine. <p>[This message has been edited by WKDFIRO (edited 04-02-2001).]||||reg||12
Z||000007||Carrolles||04-02-2001||08:28 AM||||There is no re-calibration needed for the 85 to 120 speedometer swap.  You can either change toe odometers out or reset the new one to match the old numbers.  There is a very good article on wiring changes needed to make the auxillary gauge pack work in the 85 (85s did not have the aux. gauges as an option).  You'll need this if you lose the oil pressure gauge with the old tach.||||reg||1
Z||000008||mbramble||04-02-2001||08:47 AM||||Carroles, where can I find the writeup about adding the aux guages to an 85???<P>Thanks,<BR>Mike<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000009||turbo86se||04-02-2001||10:07 AM||||thanks for the replies everyone! I appreciate it. <P>WDKFIRO, do I have to remove the speedo to alter, ooops, return the mileage to original mileage? I've got the cluster and all back in the car, and I don't plan on going through all that again any time soon. There are two toggle switches under there and lots of extra wiring for the turbo guage that I don't want to mess with again. I'd rather just swap odometers. It should read 54162, but now reads 57042. No real big deal for me, since I don't plan on ever selling this car. ||||reg||1
