Z||000013||batboy||04-02-2001||09:47 PM||||Wow, I never thought my little ralley gauge post would be so popular. DaRKLoRD has a very pretty version of my same article up on his website too.<P><BR>Yes, to get at the odometer, the instrument pod must come back out. The odometer is actually separate from the speedo.<P><BR>Yes, the factory 120 MPH speedo is a direct plug and play swap. If you use the tach that goes with the 120 MPH speedo, you lose the oil pressure gauge, hence the need for the aux. ralley gauge pod.<P><BR>There is a method of converting the old 85 MPH speedo too, but you have to replace a crystal or something and then reface the gauge with a new decal.<P><BR>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/batkid3.gif">     <B>BATBOY</B><BR>1985 SE auto with 350 Chevy V8 (Batmobile),<BR>suspension mods, lowered, GA brakes, battery<BR>relocated up front, stereo mods, etc...<p>[This message has been edited by batboy (edited 04-02-2001).]||||reg||1
